egments. The company offers engineering services to telecommunications providers, including the planning and design of aerial, underground, and buried fiber optic, copper, and coaxial cable systems; placement of cables, related structures, and drop lines for telephone companies and cable multiple system operators; program and project management, and inspection personnel; and wireless networks in connection with the deployment of macro cell and new small cell sites. It also provides construction, maintenance, and installation services, such as placement and splicing of copper, fiber, and coaxial cables; tower construction, lines and antenna installation, foundation and equipment pad construction, and small cell site placement for wireless carriers, as well as equipment installation and material fabrication, and site testing services; underground facility locating services, including locating telephone, cable television, power, water, sewer, and gas lines for utility companies; installation and maintenance of customer premise equipment for electric and gas utilities, and other customers. Dycom Industries, Inc. was incorporated in 1969 and is based in West Palm Beach, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel S. Peyovich | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $4.2M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $284K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $21K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Dycom Industries, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.4B market cap on $5.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $402M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.28\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Shares offer a 24% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 38% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Dycom Industries (DY) Is Considered a Good Investment by Brokers: Is That True?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/dycom-industries-dy-considered-good-133002086.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.861,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Does Dycom Industries (DY) Investor Investigation Mean For Shareholders?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-dy/dycom-industries/news/what-does-dycom-industries-dy-investor-investigation-mean-fo","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795637405.065,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Dycom Industries Analyst Slashes Price Target Despite Upbeat Q3","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/11/63641109/dycom-industries-analyst-slashes-price-target-despite-upbeat-q3","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795627609.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.202,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Record Backlog And Raised Outlook Could Change The Case For Dycom Industries Stock","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/r